utational-Techniques-in-Mechanical-Engineering","owner":"MunzirH","html_url":"https://github.com/MunzirH/Computational-Techniques-in-Mechanical-Engineering","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Jupyter Notebook","description":null,"topics":[],"score":224550,"global_rank":158568},{"name":"MunzirH/Applied-Parallel-Computing","owner":"MunzirH","html_url":"https://github.com/MunzirH/Applied-Parallel-Computing","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Jupyter Notebook","description":null,"topics":[],"score":224550,"global_rank":158569},{"name":"WillDittig/Fintech-Challange-Module-14","owner":"WillDittig","html_url":"https://github.com/WillDittig/Fintech-Challange-Module-14","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Jupyter Notebook","description":"In this Challenge, you\u2019ll assume the role of a financial advisor at one of the top five financial advisory firms in the world. Your firm constantly competes with the other major firms to manage and automatically trade assets in a highly dynamic environment. In recent years, your firm has heavily profited by using computer algorithms that can buy and sell faster than human traders.  The speed of these transactions gave your firm a competitive advantage early on. But, people still need to specifically program these systems, which limits their ability to adapt to new data. You\u2019re thus planning to improve the existing algorithmic trading systems and maintain the firm\u2019s competitive advantage in the market. To do so, you\u2019ll enhance the existing trading signals with machine learning algorithms that can adapt to new data.","topics":[],"score":224550,"global_rank":158577},{"name":"jerome9189/shors-algorithm","owner":"jerome9189","html_url":"https://github.com/jerome9189/shors-algorithm","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":1,"language":"Jupyter Notebook","description":"Implementation of Shor's factoring algorithm in Qiskit","topics":[],"score":224545,"global_rank":158598},{"name":"taimoorrf/wallFollowingRobot","owner":"taimoorrf","html_url":"https://github.com/taimoorrf/wallFollowingRobot","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Jupyter Notebook","description":"Python based implementation of a wall following robot using the genetic algorithm.","topics":[],"score":224545,"global_rank":158627},{"name":"shivankgoel/unbiased_reviews","owner":"shivankgoel","html_url":"https://github.com/shivankgoel/unbiased_reviews","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Jupyter Notebook","description":"Online review aggregation platforms suffer from biases which can lead to distress to both the platforms and their consumers as the average rating crowd sourced on these platforms do not represent the correct perceived quality of the product or service. We look at the problem of polarization bias on Yelp and present the evaluation of an estimation model to determine the unbiased average rating. We explore how the Yelp's elite membership program helps in cutting down the bias. Our results propose that the average biased rating listed on platforms is correlated with the true unbiased rating and by including more information from online reviews as input features of our model we can get a reasonably well\u00a0estimate of the average unbiased ratings. We propose and compare several predictive models to estimate unbiased average ratings and show how textual data can play a critical role in enhancing the predictive power. Our results can help review aggregation platforms to determine mechanisms to cut down the bias on their platforms and can benefit businesses and consumers on their platform to access a fairer metric for service quality.","topics":[],"score":224545,"global_rank":158632},{"name":"calvintirrell/smartphone_price_classification","owner":"calvintirrell","html_url":"https://github.com/calvintirrell/smartphone_price_classification","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Jupyter Notebook","description":"Determine a new smartphone's price based on similar specifications to current phone models.","topics":[],"score":224545,"global_rank":158638},{"name":"MeetTheSDE/Object-Detection","owner":"MeetTheSDE","html_url":"https://github.com/MeetTheSDE/Object-Detection","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Jupyter Notebook","description":null,"topics":[],"score":224545,"global_rank":158640},{"name":"anhhchu/DataMining","owner":"anhhchu","html_url":"https://github.com/anhhchu/DataMining","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Jupyter Notebook","description":"DataMining Tools and Techniques","topics":[],"score":224541,"global_rank":158654},{"name":"egagli/aws-rtc-10TES","owner":"egagli","html_url":"https://github.com/egagli/aws-rtc-10TES","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Jupyter Notebook","description":null,"topics":[],"score":224541,"global_rank":158670}]